/-!
# The order of vanishing on the spectrum of a principal ideal domain

Let `A` be a principal ideal domain which is not a field. The points of `Spec A` of codimension
one are exactly the ones cut out by an irreducible element, and at such a point the order of
vanishing of an element of `A`, read in the function field of `Spec A`, is the multiplicity of
that irreducible element in it.

This is the affine half of the dictionary that identifies the degree of a principal divisor on
the projective line with the arithmetic of `RatFunc k` as computed in
`StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Chow.ProperPushforwardDivisor`: for `A = k[T]` the closed points
are the monic irreducible polynomials, and `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.ord` at the point of a monic
irreducible `p` is `Stacks.Chow.ordAt p`.

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.Chow.specAlgebraMap` — the canonical ring map from `A` to the function field of
  `Spec A`, as a bundled ring homomorphism rather than through the `Algebra` instance.
* `Stacks.Chow.irreduciblePoint` — the point of `Spec A` cut out by an irreducible element.
* `Stacks.Chow.specFunctionFieldEquiv` — the function field of `Spec A` is any fraction field
  of `A`.

## Main results

* `Stacks.Chow.coheight_irreduciblePoint` — the point of an irreducible element has codimension
  one.
* `Stacks.Chow.exists_irreducible_eq_irreduciblePoint` — conversely every point of codimension
  one is the point of an irreducible element.
* `Stacks.Chow.ord_localization_eq_of_eq_pow_mul` — in the localization at the prime generated by
  an irreducible `ϖ`, the order of `ϖ ^ n * b` with `b` prime to `ϖ` is `n`.
* `Stacks.Chow.ord_irreduciblePoint_eq_of_eq_pow_mul` — the same statement on `Spec A`.
* `Stacks.Chow.ord_irreduciblePoint_eq_count` — for `A = k[T]` the order at the point of a monic
  irreducible `p` is the multiplicity of `p`, i.e. its multiplicity in the normalized
  factorization.
* `Stacks.Chow.ord_irreduciblePoint_eq_ordAt` — **the dictionary**: the order of vanishing of a
  rational function at the point of a monic irreducible `p` is `Stacks.Chow.ordAt p` of the
  corresponding element of `RatFunc k`.

## Implementation notes

### Why `Stacks.Chow.specAlgebraMap` exists

`CommRingCat.of` forks instance synthesis: the instance
`Algebra ↑R (Spec R).functionField` is found for an abstract `R : CommRingCat` and is **not**
found for `R = CommRingCat.of (Polynomial k)`, because the coercion of `CommRingCat.of` unfolds
and the discrimination tree then misses the instance. Every statement below therefore speaks of
`Stacks.Chow.specAlgebraMap`, whose type mentions no `Algebra` instance at all, so that the
statements can be instantiated at a concrete ring. The same consideration is why
`Stacks.Chow.specFunctionFieldEquiv` is a `RingEquiv` rather than an `AlgEquiv`.

### The order of vanishing through the localization

`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.ord` is defined from `Ring.ordFrac` of the stalk. The stalk of
`Spec A` at a point is the localization of `A` at the corresponding prime
(`AlgebraicGeometry.Spec.stalkIso`), and that identification carries the germ of a global section
to the image of the corresponding element of `A`
(`AlgebraicGeometry.Spec.algebraMap_stalkIso_inv`). So the computation reduces to `Ring.ord` in
the localization, which is a discrete valuation ring because `A` is a Dedekind domain, and there
the order of `ϖ ^ n * unit` is `n` (`Stacks.Chow.ord_unit_mul_pow`).

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 02RU](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/02RU)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 02MD](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/02MD)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open AlgebraicGeometry CategoryTheory Order TopologicalSpace Polynomial
